insert into public.people (id,slug,name,birth_year,death_year,birth_date,death_date,short_description,biography,why_interesting,dead_score,is_featured,status,is_fixture) values ('e4a3cdf8-b674-5990-8f15-bc94c28a2502','douglass-houghton','Douglass Houghton',1809,1845,'1809-09-21',null,'Geologist and Detroit mayor.','A New York-born scientist appointed Michigan''s first state geologist in 1839, the same year he became the University of Michigan''s first professor of geology, mineralogy, and chemistry. His 1841 survey of the Upper Peninsula''s copper deposits touched off the first major mining boom in American history, and years earlier he had personally administered more than 2,000 smallpox vaccinations to Chippewa communities during expeditions in the early 1830s. He also served a term as Detroit''s mayor in 1842, and drowned in a boating accident on Lake Superior in 1845 while surveying the region he''d helped open to development.','His copper survey triggered a mining boom, and he drowned surveying the very shoreline he''d helped make valuable.',75,false,'draft',true) on conflict (id) do nothing;
